  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Equation of tangent at <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2,4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> on the parabola <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi></math> is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br />Let the equation of the circle touching line <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math> at <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2,4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is</p><p><math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> which passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> Required circle is <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br />If <math><mi>x</mi></math> and <math><mi>y</mi></math> are integers, then</p><p><math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>2</mn></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>6</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn></math> integral points lie on the circle</p>"
  }
